                        <h2 class="nism-heading">
                            All about NISM Certificates Exam - Complete Guide (2026 Updated)
                        </h2>
<p class="about-text" style="color: #000; text-align: justify;">
    The National Institute of Securities Markets (NISM), established by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) in 2006, offers a range of certification examinations aimed at enhancing the proficiency and knowledge of professionals in the Indian securities markets. These certifications are designed for various market participants, including brokers, investment advisers, and compliance officers, among others.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-5" style="color: #0d47a1; font-size: 28px;"><strong>Mandatory vs. Non-Mandatory NISM Certification Exams
</strong></h2>

<p style="color: #000; text-align: justify;">
    With a wide range of NISM certifications available, one key question arises — <strong>which exams are mandatory</strong> for regulatory compliance, and which are <strong>voluntary</strong> for knowledge enhancement?
</p>

<h4 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">
    Mandatory NISM Exams
</h4>

<p style="color: #000; text-align: justify;">
    Certain NISM exams are <strong>required by SEBI and other regulatory bodies</strong> for professionals to work in specific roles within India’s securities markets. These are your license-to-operate exams — mandatory for jobs like mutual fund distribution, equity advisory, and portfolio management.
</p>

<p style="color: #000;"><strong>Core mandatory certifications include:</strong></p>
<ul style="color: #000;">
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series I – Currency Derivatives</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series V-A – Mutual Fund Distributors</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series VI – Depository Operations</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series VII – Securities Operations and Risk Management</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series VIII – Equity Derivatives</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series IX – Merchant Banking</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series X-A & X-B – Investment Adviser Levels 1 and 2</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series XV – Research Analyst</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series XVI – Commodity Derivatives</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series XIX-C – AIF Managers</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series XXI-A – Portfolio Management Services</li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />Series XXI-B – Portfolio Managers</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">
    Non-Mandatory NISM Exams
</h4>

<p style="color: #000; text-align: justify;">
    These exams are optional but highly recommended for professionals who want to <strong>deepen their market knowledge</strong> or enhance their career profile. While not required by regulation, they demonstrate serious intent and commitment to the field.
</p>

<p style="color: #000;"><strong>Popular non-mandatory certifications:</strong></p>
<ul style="color: #000;">
  <li>Series XII – Securities Markets Foundation</li>
  <li>Series XXIII – Social Impact Assessors</li>
  <li>Series XXIV – AML & CFT in Securities Markets</li>
</ul>

<h4 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">
    Summary
</h4>

<p style="color: #000;">
  <strong>Mandatory exams:</strong> Required for compliance and professional roles (like driving with a license).<br>
  <strong>Non-mandatory exams:</strong> Voluntary, ideal for skill-building and career differentiation.
</p>

<h3 class="mt-5" style="color: #0d47a1; font-size: 28px;"><strong>
    Discontinued NISM Certification Exams
</strong></h3>

<p style="color: #000; text-align: justify;">
    Some NISM exams have been officially withdrawn and are <strong>no longer available</strong> for enrollment or certification. If you're planning your exam schedule, make sure to refer to the latest list. Here are the certifications that have been discontinued:
</p>

<ul style="color: #000;">
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Fixed Income Securities Certification</strong> – Discontinued from <em>October 1, 2024</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Issuers Compliance Certification</strong> – Discontinued from <em>April 1, 2023</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Mutual Fund Distributors (Level 2)</strong> – Discontinued from <em>April 1, 2023</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Equity Sales Certification</strong> – Discontinued from <em>April 1, 2021</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Internal Auditors for Stock Brokers</strong> – Discontinued from <em>October 1, 2022</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Financial Education Certification</strong> – Discontinued from <em>May 15, 2024</em></li>
  <li><img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" /><strong>Taxation in Securities Markets Certification</strong> – Discontinued from <em>July 1, 2024</em></li>
</ul>

